cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HexaLogic: A Browser-Based Multi-Architecture Microcontroller Simulator"
abstract: >-
  HexaLogic is an open-source, browser-based simulation platform for the
  AT89C51/8051 and ARM microcontroller architectures, built for embedded
  systems education. It combines instruction-level discrete-event
  simulation, deterministic time-travel debugging via reverse-delta state
  capture, virtual hardware fault injection, an automated rule-based UART
  protocol analyzer, and a multi-node virtual UART network, in a single
  zero-installation environment. It extends an earlier open-source,
  single-architecture 8051 simulator (see references below) with a second
  target architecture and the capabilities described above.
